          "type": "short",
          "objective": "O4",
          "key": "Because the steps are the same every time, code can run them predictably, test them and handle an error (for example a retry or a message to the student) at lower cost, while an agent spends extra model calls and can make unexpected decisions; I would change my mind if the steps or their order varied by request in ways that cannot be listed in advance.",
